HarnessEntry(id='arc_task_8a929aca_mechanics_and_solved_layout', kind='memory', title='ARC task-8a929aca controls, completion rules, and solved layout', content='Game task-8a929aca verified across two demonstrations and one solved layout. Controls: 1=UP, 2=DOWN, 3=RIGHT, 4=LEFT. Each action moves the green 4 L-shaped object by 3 pixels. The gray 5/0 patterned L moves in the SAME direction vertically but in the OPPOSITE direction horizontally (green left => gray right; green right => gray left), also by 3 pixels. The blue b L is normally stationary but can be pushed by the green L after they overlap. Action 5 only advanced the border marker and was not needed. Goal has TWO simultaneous parts: green must exactly overlap/push-align with blue, and gray must touch/abut a boundary (outer border or central aaa divider). Successful overlap shows alternating b cells inside the green shape.\n\nSOLVED LAYOUT (fresh board): green top-left x15,y6; blue top-left x12,y51; gray top-left x42,y6; central divider x33-35; bottom border y63; right border x63. Efficient solution: DOWN 16 times (action 2), then LEFT once (action 4), total 17 actions. The first 15 downs align green and blue at y51; the 16th down pushes both to y54, putting gray at y54 adjacent to the bottom border. The final left aligns green/blue horizontally at x12; gray ends at x45,y54 and the level completes. Do NOT stop at the visual overlap at y51: it is not complete until gray also abuts a wall.\n\nGeneral strategy: calculate green moves to blue, then check gray boundary contact. If green and blue already overlap but no completion, try one more move in the green approach direction to push blue and gray toward a border. Horizontal boundary clamping can make positions confusing; prefer the direct push solution when vertical alignment permits it. Demonstration 1 route was UP x12 then LEFT x1; demonstration 2 was DOWN x6 then LEFT x4. Both finished with green/blue aligned and gray against a border/divider.', path='arc/task-8a929aca', scope='global', reference={}, arguments={}, metadata={}, source='agent', created_at='2026-11-08T10:39:34.618264+00:00', updated_at='2026-11-08T10:39:34.618281+00:00', version=1)
